      "writtenOn": "2022-11-21T14:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That sounds like the `init` section of `.so` to me. Rust doesn\u0027t have a means of moving a function there today. You would need a workaround akin to https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-life-before-main-lib-init/3855/4. I would actually be okay with that. It\u0027s memory safe, the hacky bit is just to access an OS feature not exposed by the language.",
      "parentUuid": "f8ddf16f_35350a88",
      "revId": "1de426fe333104fb45ab30ad2b5177f94d8143a5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
